{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And they shall be.</b> All the planks match each other from below — that the thickness of the rim of the two sockets should not intervene between them to separate them from each other. This is what I explained — that the hand-tenons should be gouged out from their sides, so that the width of the plank protrudes on its sides beyond the hand of the plank, to cover the rim of the socket, and so too the plank next to it — and thus they match each other. And the corner plank in the western row is gouged out along its width through its thickness, corresponding to the groove in the side of the northern and southern plank, so that the sockets should not separate them." "<b>And they shall be coupled together, whole.</b> Like 'matched.'" "<b>At its top.</b> Of the plank." "<b>To the one ring.</b> Each and every plank was gouged out at the top along its width with two grooves, on its two sides, like the thickness of a ring, and he inserts it into one ring — and thus it fits the plank next to it. But those rings — I do not know whether they are fixed or movable. And in the corner plank there was a ring in the thickness of the southern and northern plank, and the top of the corner plank in the western row enters into it — and thus the two walls are joined." "<b>So shall it be for both of them.</b> For the two planks in the corner — for the plank at the north end and for the western plank, and so too for both corners."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:54:50.464257944Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}